      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Arctic Warrior",
      "description": "ARC10170/AR62  ALASKA\nExercise Great Bear\nPvt. William F. Lansford from Stone Mountain, Georgia, USARAL Signal Company, stringing cables through the trees for communication between Mohawk CP and Fort Richardson.\n8 Feb 62\nPhoto by Sp4 Paul DeNucce\nUSARAL Spt Cmd Photo Facility\nFort Richardson\nAT465\n\nExercise Great Bear (1961-62) was a large-scale Cold War-era joint operational force-on-force military winter maneuver in Alaska, and was significant because it marked the first time in 13 years that Canadian troops had maneuvered in Alaska. It incorporated an interoperability concept with integrated conventional and Special Forces components in an austere environment.",
